---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>🚀 Agent8: Minimalist Autonomy</h1>
			<p>
				Welcome to the <strong>Agent8</strong> lab. This site is a publication surface for LLM-agent experiments and an operational toolkit designed for high-stakes reproducibility.
			</p>
			<p>
				Our core research focuses on ultra-compact shell agent designs—specifically the <strong>280-byte concept</strong>—and whether they can reliably complete complex Linux automation tasks with verifiable evidence.
			</p>
			
			<h2>Operational Roadmap</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Publication Surface:</strong> Narrative writeups and interactive experiment pages.</li>
				<li><strong>Evidence Engine:</strong> Every post is backed by immutable artifact tags, raw logs, and metric snapshots.</li>
				<li><strong>Operational Toolkit:</strong> Reusable scripts, templates, and eval utilities for the next generation of agents.</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				Every experiment published here follows a non-negotiable reproducibility protocol: exact scripts, raw CLI logs, and 100% Linux compatibility.
			</p>
			
			<p>
				Explore the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}blog`}>Archive</a> or check out our mission on the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}about`}>About</a> page.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
